{
    "background_story": "Nehemiah was a young anthropologist who had always been fascinated by the unique culture of Chilo\u00e9, a remote archipelago off the coast of Chile. He spent years studying the traditions and myths of the Chilote people, learning about their rich history and the blend of indigenous and Spanish influences. Nehemiah's research took him to the island of Lemuy, where he became particularly interested in the local legend of the Caleuche, a ghost ship said to roam the waters. As he delved deeper into the story, he began to unravel the threads of a centuries-old mystery. Nehemiah's findings sparked a new wave of interest in Chilo\u00e9's cultural heritage, and he was hailed as a leading expert in the field. His love for the island and its people had led him on a journey of discovery, shedding light on the secrets of this enchanting place.",
